title: Tibanna Prices Soar
subtitle: The gas that powers blasters and hyperdrives is suddenly scarce.
tags: event
view-if: tibanna >= 50 and tibanna_crisis_timer <= 0 and not finale and not game_ending
priority: 2
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_trade.svg
on-arrival: tibanna_crisis_timer = 8; tibanna_crises += 1

= Tibanna Prices Soar

Tibanna gas, mined in the clouds of Bespin and refined into blaster gas and hyperdrive coolant, has tripled in price. The Bespin Mining Guild blames demand; the Security Bloc blames profiteers. Every warship and every Judicial cruiser costs more to run.

*While Tibanna is scarce, defence costs more in the budget.*

- @contracts: Sign long contracts with the Bespin Mining Guild.
- @nationalise: Take over the refineries.
- @cut: Cut military purchases.

@contracts
subtitle: −1 treasury. Prices settle; the guilds profit and corruption grows.
choose-if: treasury >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The treasury cannot afford it.
on-arrival: treasury -= 1; tibanna -= 30; corruption += 1.5; guild_relation += 4

The Republic locks in supply for a decade. The Mining Guild's shareholders celebrate on Cloud City.

@nationalise
subtitle: −2 treasury. Supply is secure; the guilds are outraged and the Security Bloc approves.
choose-if: treasury >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The treasury cannot afford it.
on-arrival: treasury -= 2; tibanna -= 40; sec_relation += 4; guild_relation -= 8

Republic engineers take over the refineries in Bespin's clouds. The Mining Guild calls it theft; the Navy calls it overdue.

@cut
subtitle: Prices ease; the Republic's forces are thinner.
on-arrival: {! Q.tibanna -= 25; Q.judicial_forces -= 0.5; if (Q.war) Q.war_balance -= 0.5; Q.hawk_dissent += 3; !}

Patrols are cut back and ships stay in dock. The Hawks are appalled.
